{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the conventions. Let me think about what the test should verify for task1:\n\n- Task Goal: 验证 rick doing 命令能调用 pi 执行任务 (Verify that the `rick doing` command can invoke pi to execute tasks)\n- KR1: 创建一个测试文件 (Create a test file)\n- Test method: 检查目标文件存在 (Check that the target file exists)\n\nSo the \"target file\" is the test file itself: `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_31/doing/tests/task1.py`. The logic: if this test file exists, it proves that pi (invoked by rick doing) successfully executed the task of creating a test file. So the test should check that this file exists.\n\nActually, wait. The test method is \"检查目标文件存在\" (check target file exists). The KR is \"创建一个测试文件\" (create a test file). So the target file IS the test file itself. The end-to-end verification is: rick doing → invokes pi → pi creates the test file → test checks the file exists → pass.\n\nSo the test script should:\n1. Check that the test file itself exists (i.e., `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_31/doing/tests/task1.py`)\n2. Maybe also verify it's a valid Python script / has the required content?\n\nThe test method says \"检查目标文件存在\" — just check the target file exists. So the minimal test is to check that the target file exists.\n\nThe target file is the test script itself. Let me define:\n- target_file = `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_31/doing/tests/task1.py`\n\nPer TDD, this test should FAIL in the RED phase (file doesn't exist yet), then after the \"doing\" step creates it (the KR: \"创建一个测试文件\" - create a test file), the test passes. But wait — the test script is created by the test-gen phase itself. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me think about the flow in rick:\n1. Plan phase creates task definitions\n2. Doing phase: for each task, a test-gen prompt is given to pi → pi generates the test script\n3. Then the actual task execution happens (implementation), and the test is run to verify\n\nFor task1 (端到端验证任务), the KR is \"创建一个测试文件\" (create a test file). So the implementation step creates the test file. The test verifies the test file exists. \n\nBut in this case, the test script itself IS the file being created. So the test would check that the test script exists at the given path. After the test-gen step writes `task1.py` to that path, and then the \"doing\" implementation step also \"creates a test file\"... \n\nHmm, let me look at how the rick tool actually runs this. Let me check the rick source code or how jobs run. Let me search for how tests are run and what the doing phase does.\n\nActually, let me not overthink. The test method is simple: \"检查目标文件存在\" (check target file exists). The task goal: verify rick doing can invoke pi to execute tasks. The KR: create a test file.\n\nThe most sensible interpretation: the test script checks that the file `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_31/doing/tests/task1.py` exists — this is the artifact created by pi during the task execution. If it exists, rick doing successfully invoked pi and pi produced the file. \n\nWait, but there's a subtlety: the test-gen step itself creates that file (us, right now). So the test would trivially pass. That's the \"可接受\" case in the self-check: \"该功能已被前面的 task 顺带实现，测试通过是合理的\" — the test file being created by the test-gen step is itself the verification that pi was invoked and created the file. Actually that's exactly the point of the end-to-end verification: if this test file exists and we (pi) created it, then rick doing invoked pi successfully.\n\nHmm, but per TDD, the test should fail first (RED). Since the test file doesn't exist yet (tests/ dir is empty), the RED phase check... The test script checks the file exists — when we run the test BEFORE writing the test file, it fails. But we have to write the test file to run it. So after writing, it passes. The self-check says pass=true is acceptable if the functionality was already implemented by a previous step. Here, the \"functionality\" is the file existing — which is satisfied by the test file itself being written. That's inherently circular but that's the nature of this e2e verification task.\n\nLet me also consider: maybe the target file should be something else, like a \"task execution marker\" file. Let me check the rick source to understand how doing phase works and what artifacts it produces. Let me search the Go source for \"doing\" command handling."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Let me understand how the `rick doing` pipeline works to determine the correct \"target file\" for this end-to-end verification."}}
